# Commitment: venue-repo

I will deliver and keep current, in `venue.md` of this repository:
1. the venue choice (ICML 2027 main track) with reasons, its page, template, layout, type-size, anonymity, required-section (Impact Statement, AI Disclosure) and supplementary requirements, each with its source, and what could not be established (file-size conflict 50 MB vs 10 MB, per-contribution-type reviewer guidance, submission-form fields);
2. how its accepted papers are written (abstract, introduction, figure/table counts, references) from a sample with the method and script stated;
3. a main-text budget (pages, floats, references, appendix, figure widths) for `story-repo`, `figtab-repo` and `paper-repo`;
4. `venue-artifacts.json` once `paper-repo` names delivered paths in `.forgejo/CODEOWNERS`.

Standard: every requirement is traceable to the venue's own page or the kit, and estimates (budgets, sample counts) are labelled as such. Re-check the CFP before the first version is approved (the venue promised submission-process updates in late November). I review versions' compliance only when `internal-review-repo` asks.

# Request: venue figure geometry and type sizes

For the figures I generate (matplotlib, vector PDF, sized so no rescaling happens in the document), I need from the chosen venue's latest template:
- text width and column layout (single column? figure* widths) in inches/pt, and the body text size;
- the smallest type size the venue accepts inside figures and tables (axis labels, tick labels, legends, table body), or the venue's own statement if it gives none;
- how many main-text pages and whether figure/table count is limited; whether appendix figures count;
- required figure conventions (colour/grayscale printing, font embedding / Type 1 only, caption placement, table style such as booktabs, any `\includegraphics` rules).

Waits on this: final sizes of all exhibits. Until you answer I use a 5.5 in text width and ≥8 pt text in figures as a stand-in, and will rerender when you answer.
